# Firebase (PRD §4.1) is @react-native-firebase/*: the native SDKs read
# credential FILES, not env vars. There are no EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_* values.
#
#   Android   apps/mobile/google-services.json
#   iOS       apps/mobile/GoogleService-Info.plist
#
# Both are git-ignored (PRD §16). Download them from the Firebase console
# (Project settings -> Your apps) and drop them next to app.config.ts for a
# local build. For EAS builds, upload each ONCE as a file-type environment
# variable per environment (development / preview / production), which
# eas.json maps to each build profile:
#
#   eas env:create --scope project --environment preview \
#       --name GOOGLE_SERVICES_JSON --type file --value ./google-services.json
#   eas env:create --scope project --environment preview \
#       --name GOOGLE_SERVICES_PLIST --type file --value ./GoogleService-Info.plist
#
# EAS exposes each as an absolute path in the env var of the same name;
# app.config.ts reads them. With NEITHER file present the app still builds and
# boots into the §12.4 offline path.
#
# HOW TO TELL, on a preview APK: §7.11's real Home replaced the Stage-0 debug
# status line, so there is no longer a "Firebase: not configured" label to
# read. Use the analytics debug overlay instead — it is already gated on
# EXPO_PUBLIC_DEV_BOARD, which the preview profile sets. Events sitting in the
# queue undelivered means no native Firebase app; events draining means the
# credential file was picked up.
#
# MIXED CASE: one @react-native-firebase/app plugin entry registers BOTH
# platforms' mods, so uploading only GOOGLE_SERVICES_JSON leaves `eas build -p
# ios` and a bare `expo prebuild` throwing on the missing plist. `eas build -p
# android` runs android mods only and is fine — and Android-only is the real
# Stage-1 state, since the plist needs the Apple Developer account CLAUDE.md
# records as deferred.
#
# eas.json's `cli.version: ">= 12.0.0"` floor is CORRECT for the build-profile
# `environment` key used below — verified against the registry: eas-cli 12.0.0
# bundles @expo/eas-json 12.0.0, which already declares
# `environment?: 'preview' | 'production' | 'development'` with the same type
# as current releases. A QA audit suspected the floor predated the key and
# flagged it as unverifiable without network; it does not.
